  <revision rev="7" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>e47eeeb9575c3349c4a25467c53d4a49</srcmd5>
    <version>0.19.0</version>
    <time>1762536161</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to 0.19.0:
  * Improve JSON encoding performance by up to 40%.
  * Ensure tuple and frozenset default values are treated identically whether
    specified by value or default_factory.
  * Fix memory leak of match_args in StructConfig object.
  * Fix memory leak in Raw.copy().
  * Update decode signatures for PEP 688.
  * Generate __replace__ method on Struct types, for use with copy.replace.
  * Fix incorrect decoding of certain &gt; 64 bit integers.
  * Call __post_init__ when converting from an object to a Struct.
  * BREAKING: Expand buffer when encode_into is passed a buffer smaller than
    offset.
  * Support Raw objects as inputs to convert.
  * Error nicely when a dataclass type (instead of an instance) is passed to
    encode.
  * Drop support for Python 3.8.
  * Add support for Python 3.13.
  * Remove deprecated from_builtins.
  * Support encoding any Enum type whose .value is a supported type.
  * Don't fail eagerly when processing generic types with unsupported
    __parameters__.
  * Use eval_type_backport to backport type annotations to Python 3.9.
- Drop patch python313.patch, included upstream.
- Add patch support-python314.patch:
  * Support Python 3.14 annontation changes.</comment>
    <requestid>1316366</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="8" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>b550e0e31f6846d6e5b57cf789eb5b02</srcmd5>
    <version>0.21.1</version>
    <time>1794236634</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- update to 0.21.1:
  * Fix `ValidationError` and `DecodeError` raised in `dec_hook`
    being incorrectly wrapped in another `ValidationError`
  * Fix a potential `NULL` dereference in
    `structmeta_get_module_ns` ({pr}`1016`).
  * Fix a reference leak in `ms_passes_big_int_constraints`
  * Fix missing `ref_template` parameter in `msgspec.json.schema`
    type stub ({pr}`1002`).
  * Clarify `order='deterministic'` encoder docstrings
  * Add a porting guide for users migrating from orjson
  * Fix a segfault on Python 3.13+ that could occur when creating
    structs that contained a
  * `__dict__`, instead of only using `__slots__` ({pr}`960`).
  * Improve type annotations for `msgspec.UNSET` ({pr}`975`).
  * Fix hashing of decoded tuples on Python 3.14 ({pr}`980`).
  * Add `ref_template` arg to `msgspec.json.schema` ({pr}`983`).
  * Add missing `libm` linkage to some architectures ({pr}`993`).
  * Fix memory leak when decoding sets ({pr}`991`).
  * Add `uniqueItems` annotation to `set`/`frozenset` JSON
    schemas ({pr}`984`).

- update to 0.20.0:
  * Support Python 3.14, including freethreaded mode ({pr}`852`,
    {pr}`877`).
  * Expose the `StructMeta` metaclass ({pr}`890`, {pr}`927`,
    {pr}`928`, {pr}`940`, {pr}`945`).
  * Add `msgspec.inspect.is_struct` and
    `msgspec.inspect.is_struct_type` functions for checking
    whether an object is a `msgspec.Struct`-like instance or
    class ({pr}`950`).</comment>
    <requestid>1396182</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="9" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>264d9bb1495bc4a01d124337a77ebac7</srcmd5>
    <version>0.22.0</version>
    <time>1795704867</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to 0.22.0:
  * Raise ValueError when setting gc=False on a struct with a weakref slot
  * Add frozendict support on Python 3.15+ and PyEmscripten support
  * Support callable decimal_format in JSON and MessagePack Encoders
  * Support Literal[True] and Literal[False] types
  * Fix PEP 695 type parameter syntax and types.GenericAlias in annotations
  * Fix NameError creating a Struct with unquoted forward refs on Python 3.14
  * Fix crash on invalid ClassVar and AttributeError when missing __name__
  * Fix overriding an inherited field alias back to the field's own name
  * Raise ValidationError on out-of-range int to float conversion
  * Improve expected-type names in validation errors for Raw fields
  * Fix out-of-range Meta bound error messages and add Meta stub overloads
  * Fix reference leaks in msgpack Ext decoding, to_builtins, and encoders
  * Fix JSON schema generation for mixed Literals, optional unions,
    array_like=True structs, and set/bytearray default factories
  * Preserve JSON Schema metadata in propertyNames for annotated dict keys
  * Fix json.encode failing for dicts keyed by str-valued Enum
  * Fix missing GC traversal, allocation error handling, and Python 3.15
    compilation warnings
  * Report leading encode/decode arg as positional-only in inspect.signature
  * Update type stubs across encoders, decoders, and annotations</comment>
    <requestid>1400683</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
